    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0780" n="760" xml:id="pg760"/>

                <head>326. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Vietnam<anchor n="1" xml:id="d326-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-12-08T14:02:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1962—2:02 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>588. Embtel 567.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d326-f2"
                    /> In Departmentʼs view political considerations would suggest limiting use
                    napalm to high priority targets which clearly VC
                    installations. Assume this has been past policy and that similar discretion will
                    be employed in future.</p>
                <p>Also request Embassy report to Department on pros and cons use napalm in Viet-Nam
                    with particular emphasis on question whether such use will damage GVNʼs eventual ability reestablish its influence in
                    areas subjected to it.</p>
                <p>In future, plans for using large amounts napalm in any one operation to be
                    cleared with Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d326-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d326-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 751K.00/12-562. Secret. Drafted by
                        Wood on December 7, cleared with
                        Cottrell and DOD/ISA, and initialed by Harriman Repeated to CINCPAC for Polad.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d326-f2" n="2" xml:id="d326-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 567, December 5, reported that Harkins had obtained JCS authority contingent upon Embassy
                    concurrence, to utilize Farmgate aircraft to deliver napalm in an air operation
                    in Zone D. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
